# Git push

Do not run `git push github` yourself. Use `scripts/publish.sh` from a clean `main` after tests pass. It runs the private-path leak check, `pytest tests`, bumps the patch in `pyproject.toml` with a `chore: release` commit (skipped when that commit is already `HEAD`), then pushes `main` to the public GitHub remote `github` only. It refuses the retired public GitLab URL `git@gitlab.com:meine-group4/kaufen-oder-mieten.git`. Never push the `private` branch to a public remote.

Use `scripts/backup.sh` only for the private `backup` remote (`main` and `private`). It refuses URLs that match public `github` or the retired public GitLab project. Set `git remote add backup <private-url>` or `BUY_VS_RENT_BACKUP_REMOTE`; do not invent a URL.

Do not push failing tests, secrets, or half-finished work.

If the environment blocks push to protected `main`, retry with approval or tell the user the branch is ahead of a public remote.
